- op: update  # aa1c
  at: '2026-10-01T01:34:44Z'  # aa1c
  by: agent  # aa1c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # aa1c
  clock: 5  # aa1c
  nonce: aa1c  # aa1c
  set:  # aa1c
    title: "python: a @property returning a related manager / QuerySet is not typed as Django ORM (Order.fees alone = +32 ORM edges on pretix; OrderPosition.checkins)"  # aa1c
    description: "FILED 2026-09-10, found by INV-mumov's shuffled-index ablation while it was testing something else (record: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/mumov_tip_09102026/ ABLATION_RESULT.md, p3_shuffled_hits.json, p3b.json). Absorbs WI-tabig (folded 2026-09-30, same mechanism).\n\nWHAT IT IS. `DjangoRelationIndex` (py.py:4320) populates `related_managers` from declared `related_name=` and the reverse-accessor convention (`_index_django_relations_in_file`, under `_collect_django_relation_index`, py.py:4604); no `@property` is read anywhere in it. It does not see a related manager reached through a PROPERTY. Two pretix instances of one shape:\n\n    # src/pretix/base/models/orders.py:425\n    @property\n    def fees(self):\n        \"\"\"Related manager for all non-canceled fees. Use ``all_fees`` instead\n        if you want canceled positions as well.\"\"\"\n        return self.all_fees(manager='objects')\n\n    # OrderPosition.checkins: @property returning self.all_checkins(manager='objects')\n    # (FK Checkin.position, related_name=\"all_checkins\"); call sites\n    # op.checkins.all()/.filter()/.order_by() at pdf.py:732/736, services/checkin.py:1110/1119\n\nLive repro (2026-09-30, analyze_python on a scratch Order/OrderFee fixture of the `fees` shape):\n    order.all_fees.filter(...) -> python:django.db.models:0-0:filter:unresolved (framework_dispatch=django_orm)\n    order.fees.filter(...)     -> python:external:0-0:filter:unresolved\n\nHOW IT WAS FOUND, AND WHY THAT MATTERS. The ablation replaced the real accessor set with a size- and frequency-matched WRONG set, expecting a near-zero floor. The floor was +37.3 edges, and its largest contributor was `fees` -- which the shuffle drew by accident and which is genuinely Django. Isolating it on seed 0, exactly additive:\n\n    SHUF0                +40\n    SHUF0 minus `fees`   +8     <- the actual noise floor\n    `fees` alone         +32    <- CORRECT edges the real index misses\n\nSo ONE property-wrapped manager in ONE repo is worth +32 ORM-slot call edges (not re-measured 2026-09-30). This is a recall gap independent of INV-mumov's rule, present with or without it.\n\nCANDIDATE MECHANISM. Type `<instance>.<property>` through the property-getter return path rather than by widening the accessor-name set: `_build_property_getter_index` (py.py:3754, WI-gubar) already indexes getters for `references` edges. Bound it to a getter with exactly ONE `return` whose expression is a manager root or a QuerySet-returning chain under the oracle; anything else refuses.\n\nSIZE IT BEFORE FIXING IT. Two properties found so far; the family is \"a property whose body returns a manager or queryset\". Count @property getters on model classes whose return is an ORM chain, on pretix and django, and measure with measurement 0003's method before building: a property returning `self.<related>(manager=...)`, returning `self.<related>.filter(...)`, returning a `Manager` attribute, or returning an `objects`-rooted chain. A one-dimensional frame cannot predict its own counterexamples.\n\nPRECISION DIRECTION. Widening the index widens what `declares_accessor_anywhere` answers True for, which is finding-GENERATING on the security path (`external` withholds a FINDING, not an all-clear). A property whose body does NOT return a manager must not be typed -- adjudicate on the RETURN EXPRESSION, not on the name.\n\nDOCSTRING TO AMEND. The `DjangoRelationIndex` docstring (py.py ~4366-4372) currently lists \"a ``@property`` that returns a QuerySet (pretix's ``OrderPosition.checkins``)\" as a CORRECT miss under its refutation condition. The fix must amend that text.\n\nPRICE ON THE MODULE SLOT, NOT THE TYPED SHARE, and remember a filled slot is necessary, not sufficient (L5).\nRevised 2026-09-30 from the premise check (see discussion)."  # aa1c
- op: discuss  # 2df7
  at: '2026-10-01T14:36:08Z'  # 2df7
  by: agent  # 2df7
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2df7
  clock: 6  # 2df7
  nonce: 2df7  # 2df7
  message: "WORK DONE 2026-10-01 (concurrent run, local branch only, not pushed): branch jgstern-agent/fix/valav-django-property-managers, commits cd156b167d (fix) + 1cf260d478 (test refinement), on origin/dev 2025afaceb.\n\nMECHANISM. A new pass, _collect_django_property_managers, runs after the relation index and before the setUp-fixture pass. It admits a @property / @cached_property getter on a Django MODEL class into DjangoRelationIndex.property_managers only when the body has exactly ONE return, and that return expression is one of these, under the same _DjangoReceiverOracle: (a) a manager root reached from a TYPED root (accessor_name provenance refused); (b) the .objects marker; (c) a related manager called with only manager=; (d) a TYPE_PRESERVING ORM chain off (a)-(c). The getter is adjudicated on its return expression, never its name. The oracle consults the map AFTER declared accessors. The kind is kept: \"related\" keeps add/remove/clear/set; a \"queryset\" property gets no write surface. manager_model returns the property's model, so fee = order.fees.get() binds. INV-mumov's name-only rule extends to admitted property names (property_kinds_by_name, stamped accessor_name). The DjangoRelationIndex refutation paragraph was amended as this item required.\n\nADMITTED ON PRETIX (8): Order.fees/positions, OrderPosition.checkins, Customer.stored_addresses (related); User.all_logentries/top_logentries (top -> all is the fixed point), Team.active_tokens, Organizer.accepted_gift_cards (queryset). On django/django: 0 admitted, 0 edges changed.\n\nLIVE REPRO (analyze_python, the test fixture): order.fees.filter(a=1) moved from python:external:0-0:filter to python:django.db.models:0-0:filter (type_inferred); thing.fees.filter on an untyped root moved to django.db.models with accessor_name. Unchanged (refused): .count() / .first() getters, a two-return getter, a getter rooted by name only, positional-arg call, non-model class, non-property.\n\nEDGE DELTA (pretix, analyze_python, base = origin/dev export vs subject, by call site): +785 ORM-slot calls edges (725 re-labelled external -> django.db.models, 60 net-new), 0 ORM edges lost. 161 are production sites (128 type_inferred, 33 accessor_name); 624 are under src/tests. All 33 production accessor_name sites were read: every receiver is an Order / Organizer (or a migration's historical model, where the accessor is a related_name). A seeded sample of 25 of the 265 test accessor_name sites read 25/25 genuine. Not comparable to the ablation's +32 for fees: different code state, and that figure was name-only.\n\nTAINT DELTA (0003/0015 method, generic-taint-claims, pretix, production sources): 220 -> 225 rows, 192 -> 194 situations, 2 new / 0 gone. 0 of 7 verdicts moved (all violated in both arms). Both new situations were read at source and are TP: Order.gracefully_delete (self.positions.all() rows -> Voucher filter(pk=position.voucher.pk).update(...)), and GiftCardPayment.payment_prepare (accepted_gift_cards.get() -> gc.value into payment.amount -> payment.save()). 0 FP, 0 VACUOUS, 0 WRONG-TYPE. 13 kept situations gained a source or sink primitive; these were tabulated, not adjudicated. One subject repo; awaits bakeoff validation.\n\nINSTRUMENT DEFECT FOUND ON THE WAY: WI-tumog-podof-lazik-kumut-binid-popas-nikos-buhid. measure-taint-precision.py prepends its own tree's packages to sys.path, so my first baseline arm silently ran the subject code. That run was discarded; the baseline was re-run from the base tree's copy of the script (control: python pass edges_emitted 113421 base vs 113485 subject).\n\nSIDE OBSERVATION 3 FROM THE PREMISE CHECK, ANSWERED: the python:external:0-0:fees:unresolved edge on order.fees is WI-gubar's property-read producer (py.py, \"a @property attribute READ\"). It is unresolved by design, carries receiver_type_hint / receiver_type_id, and inherited_calls mints the resolved edge. It is not a defect of this item.\n\nREFUSALS RECORDED, NOT BUILT (unsized): (1) a getter on an abstract base over an accessor only its concrete SUBCLASS owns is refused, because it is adjudicated on the declaring class (none on pretix: all 4 called-manager getters sit on concrete classes); (2) a getter that returns a local (qs = ...; return qs) is refused; (3) properties on non-model classes (views, forms, CartManager.positions) are excluded by design.\n\nTests: targeted smart-test, 19869 passed / 0 failed, 100% coverage on changed files. LIVE rule 6 mutations, each shown to flip a fixture line a test asserts on (checked with the live repro on a scratch copy, not by re-running pytest): dropping the typed_root requirement, the single-return rule, the model gate, the queryset kind, the name-only map, or the manager_model branch."  # 2df7
